# THE LIVE SITE IS ON NETLIFY (checked 18 Nov 2026: responses carry
# x-nf-request-id and "Netlify Edge"; it's published from Bolt). This file is
# what actually runs. vercel.json says the same things for Vercel, kept in case
# the site ever moves there; keep the two in step.
#
# Netlify serves a real file first when one exists; these rules cover paths
# with no file. Order matters: first match wins.

# The old quiz addresses now go to the one application form (18 Nov 2026).
# Its quiz only asked for $5k; the new form has the £10k rule. Query strings
# (utm_source, ad_id, fbclid) are carried over.
/apply      /start      301
/en/apply   /en/start   301
/uz/apply   /uz/start   301

# The Round 3 ad landing page has its own lightweight entry (start.html), so a
# phone on mobile data loads only the form, not the whole site.
/start      /start.html  200
/en/start   /start.html  200
/uz/start   /start.html  200

# The Meta instant form's thank-you page (25 Nov 2026): a plain file that
# sends the lead on to dad's WhatsApp. See public/whatsapp.html.
/whatsapp      /whatsapp.html  200
/en/whatsapp   /whatsapp.html  200

# Everything else is the single-page site.
/*  /index.html  200
